### Contextual states

Set the `state` prop on `<gl-form-checkbox>` or `<gl-form-checkbox-group>` to `false` (invalid), `true` (valid), or `null` (no validation state):

- `false` suits a blocking or required field that a user has to fix before the form can be submitted.
- `true` suits a form that validates each field as the user goes, to confirm this one is fine.
- `null` shows no validation state.

The prop sets `aria-invalid` on the input, but the checkbox keeps its usual colors. Wrap it in a [form group](https://design.gitlab.com/components/form-group) with `invalid-feedback` or `valid-feedback` to give the state a message a sighted user can see:

```text
<script>
  export default {
    data() {
      return {
        accepted: false,
      };
    },
  };
</script>

{{ govukErrorSummary({
  titleText: "There is a problem",
  errorList: [
    {
      text: "Enter your full name",
      href: "#"
    },
    {
      text: "The date your passport was issued must be in the past",
      href: "#"
    }
  ]
}) }}
```

